    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="0856" n="846" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg846"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.0031/4–2949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-29T20:00:00+01:00">April 29, 1949—8
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 29—4:18 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1661. Received Deptel 1382, April 22. Tomlinson,<anchor n="28" xml:id="d798-f1"/>
                    Foreign Office, states decision at highest level required. British apparently
                    particularly worried re application policy Hong Kong and had awaited recent
                    arrival UK trade commissioner that colony in order discuss this aspect.</p>
                <p>Foreign Office cannot indicate definite date when final decision possible but
                    will expedite consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d798-f1" n="28" xml:id="d798-f1-content">
                <p>Frank S. Tomlinson of the Far Eastern Department, British Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
